{
 "_about": "Grammar rules for Dhivehi, built from corpus counts. These target the errors an LLM makes most often when writing Dhivehi. They are checked by dhivehi_rules/dba_rules.py (grammar_check) whenever a context is given, or with --grammar, and they always run in dhivehi_rules/script_gate.py. Without a context or --grammar they do not run, so the default spelling and word-division output is unchanged. Each rule has corpus evidence: news (26 crawled news sites), 469 public speeches and 93k Majlis sittings. See guides/grammar.md. severity 'error' means do not ship. 'warn' is reported with a leading ~; judge it in context. 'replace' is an re.Match.expand() template for the suggested form.",
 "existential": {
  "_about": "Agreement between a noun and the existential/locative verb: ހުރި (standing things, physical objects, most plurals), އޮތް (abstract and lying things: ފުރުސަތު, ސުވާލު, ހައްލު...), ތިބި (animate plurals: people, a group). The verb is checked against the noun right before it (predicate: 'ސުވާލެއް ހުރި') and, for a bare participle, the noun right after it (relative: 'ހުރި ސުވާލެއް'). Number matters: ސުވާލެއް takes އޮތް but ސުވާލުތައް takes ހުރި. 'nouns' maps a key to raw corpus counts per number (sgi = indefinite singular -އެއް; sg = bare; pl = -ތައް/-ތަކެއް/-ތަކެތި, or a human plural in -ން) and position. A use is flagged when the corpus prefers one verb for that slice with share >= min_share over at least min_n uses, and the verb used has share <= max_used_share. It is an error when the preferred share is >= error_share and n >= error_n; otherwise it is a warning. The key is the noun with the number suffix and a final ު/ް removed, as in the miner.",
  "thresholds": {
   "min_n": 30,
   "min_share": 0.8,
   "max_used_share": 0.1,
   "error_share": 0.9,
   "error_n": 100
  },
